LAB 05 – Shift Log Analysis (Parsing & Data Processing)
Aim
To read production shift logs, extract useful information and generate a quality inspection report.
Key Concepts
String Handling: strip() removes unwanted spaces.
Split Function: split() separates log data into fields.
Type Conversion: float() converts diameter values into numerical form.
Upper Function: Converts shift names into uppercase.
List: Stores multiple diameter readings.
Data Analysis: Calculates count, average, minimum and maximum values.
Filtering: Separates parts into ACCEPT, REWORK and SCRAP categories.
Sets: Compares day and night shift scrap codes to identify common and unique parts.
Important Learning
A string and a number are different data types.
Extra spaces can create errors during data processing.
Lists are useful for storing multiple production readings.
Result
Learned to process production log data and prepare a shift-wise quality report.
